        <h2 class="useful-subtitle">General Useful Information</h2>

        <div class="general-useful-cards">

            <div class="general-useful-card">
                <h3>Visas</h3>
                <p>
                    Citizens of EU member states, Schengen Agreement countries, Andorra, Montenegro,
                    Liechtenstein, Monaco, San Marino, Serbia, the Holy See and Switzerland can travel
                    to Bosnia and Herzegovina with a travel document or a valid ID card.
                </p>
                <p>
                    The minimum amount of money for foreigners traveling to Bosnia and Herzegovina is
                    150.00 BAM for each day of intended stay.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="general-useful-card">
                <h3>Working Hours</h3>
                <p>
                    Most public offices work Monday to Friday from 08:00 to 16:00.
                    Banks are usually open until 18:00 on weekdays and until 13:00 on Saturdays.
                </p>
                <p>
                    Stores usually stay open until 20:00, while shopping centres are usually open until 22:00.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="general-useful-card">
                <h3>Official Language</h3>
                <p>
                    Bosnian, Croatian and Serbian are spoken in Sarajevo. Many people also understand
                    basic communication in English and German.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="general-useful-card">
                <h3>Time Zone</h3>
                <p>Bosnia and Herzegovina and Sarajevo are in the Central European Time Zone, GMT +1.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="general-useful-card">
                <h3>Currency</h3>
                <p>
                    The official currency is the convertible mark, BAM. Bills of 10, 20, 50, 100 and
                    200 BAM are in circulation, as well as coins of 1, 2 and 5 BAM.
                </p>
                <p>1 BAM has 100 convertible pfennigs.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="general-useful-card">
                <h3>Credit Cards</h3>
                <p>
                    Most stores and restaurants accept American Express, Diners, Mastercard and Visa.
                    In many cafes, crafts, parking areas and city transport, cash payment is often needed.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="general-useful-card">
                <h3>Tax Free Shopping</h3>
                <p>
                    Foreign nationals leaving Bosnia and Herzegovina are entitled to a VAT refund.
                    The minimum invoice amount eligible for VAT refund is 100.00 BAM.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="general-useful-card">
                <h3>Road Rules</h3>
                <p>
                    Permissible speeds are 60 km/h in settlements, 80 km/h outside settlements and
                    120 km/h on highways. Winter driving rules apply from November to April.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="general-useful-card">
